@geindex HandlePretty() (pyGHDL.cli.dom.Application method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL cli dom pyGHDL cli dom Application HandlePretty}@anchor{1e3}
@deffn {Method} HandlePretty (args)

Handle the @code{pretty} sub-command: translate the selected sources and write each document as VHDL code.

A file is translated on its own; a directory is scanned, and each subdirectory is reported as a library of that
name. The documents aren’t added to the design, nor analyzed. Each document is written by
VHDLWriter@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Formatting.VHDL.html#pyVHDLModel.Formatting.VHDL.VHDLWriter}: its design units with their context items, in source order.
The time `libghdl' spent parsing and the time the translation took are reported per file.

A file, that can’t be translated or written, is reported as an error; the remaining files are written. The
application exits with an error, if an error was reported.

@*Parameters: 
@code{args} – The parsed arguments, carrying the selected files, directory, default library, VHDL version and tab
size.

@end deffn

