@geindex PrintMissingDependencyError() (pyGHDL.cli.dom.Application method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL cli dom pyGHDL cli dom Application PrintMissingDependencyError}@anchor{1ff}
@deffn {Method} PrintMissingDependencyError (ex)

Print a missing optional dependency and the command lines installing it.

Unlike the other printers, this one does `not' report a bug: there is no traceback, and no invitation to
open an issue, because nothing is wrong with the program - a package it can use is not installed. The message
names the missing package and every installation option the exception carries
(@code{InstallCommands}).

@cartouche
@quotation Attention 
A dependency missing while a module is imported raises before an application object exists, so this method
cannot report that case. An application that wants to survive it catches the exception around its own imports
and prints the commands directly:

@example
from pyTooling.Exceptions import MissingDependencyError

try:
  from myPackage.Plotting import Plot
except MissingDependencyError as ex:
  print(f"@{ex@}\n" + "\n".join(f"  @{command@}" for command in ex.InstallCommands))
  raise SystemExit(MissingDependencyError.EXIT_CODE) from ex
@end example
@end quotation
@end cartouche

@*Parameters: 
@code{ex} (@code{MissingDependencyError}) – The exception to print.


@*Return type: 
NoReturn@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.NoReturn}


@*Returns: 
Never - the method exits the application with @ref{1fe,,MISSING_DEPENDENCY_EXIT_CODE}.



@subsubheading See also



@table @asis

@item @ref{202,,PrintException()}

→ Print an unhandled exception and its traceback.

@item @ref{204,,PrintNotImplementedError()}

→ Print a call to an unimplemented function or abstract method.
@end table

@end deffn

