@deffn {Method} _PrintVersion (packageName=None, versionCheckTimeout=1)

Helper method to print the version information.

The author(s), email, copyright, version and URLs are read from the dunder variables of the module the class
constant @ref{1dc,,DUNDER_MODULE} refers to. If it is @code{None}, every dunder variable counts as missing.

@*Parameters: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{packageName} (Optional@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Optional}[str@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str}]) – Optional, name of the package on PyPI. If given, the latest released version is
queried and reported as an available update. Default: @code{None}.

@item 
@code{versionCheckTimeout} (int@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int}) – Optional, timeout in seconds for the PyPI request. Default: @code{1}.
@end itemize


@*Raises: 
TypeError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#TypeError} – If parameter ‘packageName’ is not of type str@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str}. 
A module with dunder variables is set as class constant @ref{1dc,,DUNDER_MODULE}.


@*Return type: 
None@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#None}


@cartouche
@quotation Example usage 
@example
import myPackage

class Application(TerminalApplication):
  HEADLINE =      "My Application"
  DUNDER_MODULE = myPackage

  def HandleVersion(self, _: Namespace) -> None:
    self._PrintHeadline()
    self._PrintVersion("myPackage")
@end example
@end quotation
@end cartouche
@end deffn

