@geindex ConcurrentBlockStatement (class in pyGHDL.dom.Concurrent)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Concurrent pyGHDL dom Concurrent ConcurrentBlockStatement}@anchor{304}
@deffn {Class} pyGHDL.dom.Concurrent.ConcurrentBlockStatement (blockNode, label, genericItems=None, genericAssociationItems=None, portItems=None, portAssociationItems=None, declaredItems=None, statements=None, documentation=None)

This class implements a @ref{3,,pyGHDL.dom} object derived from pyVHDLModel.Concurrent.ConcurrentBlockStatement@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Concurrent.html#pyVHDLModel.Concurrent.ConcurrentBlockStatement}.

Represents a block statement.

A block groups concurrent statements (@ref{3df,,Statements}) and may declare its own items
(@ref{3e0,,DeclaredItems}). It always forms a hierarchy level; independently of that, it may also have
a block header: a generic clause (@ref{3e1,,GenericItems}) with its generic map aspect
(@ref{3e2,,GenericAssociationItems}), and a port clause (@ref{3e3,,PortItems}) with its port map aspect
(@ref{3e4,,PortAssociationItems}).

@cartouche
@quotation Example 
@example
  blk : block
--^^^                              <- Label
    generic (G : positive := 1);
--          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^     <- GenericItems
    generic map (G => 2);
--              ^^^^^^^^           <- GenericAssociationItems
    port (bp : in bit);
--        ^^^^^^^^^^^              <- PortItems
    port map (bp => clock);
--           ^^^^^^^^^^^^          <- PortAssociationItems
    signal inner : bit := '0';
--  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^     <- DeclaredItems
  begin
    inner <= bp;
--  ^^^^^^^^^^^^                   <- Statements
  end block;
@end example
@end quotation
@end cartouche


