@geindex ProcessStatement (class in pyGHDL.dom.Concurrent)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Concurrent pyGHDL dom Concurrent ProcessStatement}@anchor{305}
@deffn {Class} pyGHDL.dom.Concurrent.ProcessStatement (processNode, label=None, declaredItems=None, statements=None, sensitivityList=None, documentation=None)

This class implements a @ref{3,,pyGHDL.dom} object derived from pyVHDLModel.Concurrent.ProcessStatement@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Concurrent.html#pyVHDLModel.Concurrent.ProcessStatement}.

Represents a process statement.

A process declares its own items (@ref{473,,DeclaredItems}) and groups sequential statements
(@ref{474,,Statements}). It may name a sensitivity list (@ref{475,,SensitivityList}).

@cartouche
@quotation Example 
@example
  proc : process (clock)
--^^^^                     <- optional Label
--                ^^^^^    <- optional SensitivityList
    variable v : bit;
--  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^      <- DeclaredItems
  begin
    v := '1';
--  ^^^^^^^^^              <- Statements
  end process;
@end example
@end quotation
@end cartouche

