@geindex RemoveDeclaredItem() (pyGHDL.dom.Concurrent.IfGenerateBranch method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Concurrent pyGHDL dom Concurrent IfGenerateBranch RemoveDeclaredItem}@anchor{4da}
@deffn {Method} RemoveDeclaredItem (declaredItem)

Remove a declared item from the declarative region.

The declared item is detached: its parent is cleared. If the region is indexed, the declared item’s identifiers are
removed from the region’s namespace and from the lookup table matching its kind first; they are checked before
anything is changed. The declared item itself is unchanged and can be added to another declarative region, or
inserted at another position.

The namespace refers to the overload declared last: removing it, the namespace refers to the remaining overload
declared last. If another declaration shares an identifier with the declared item (e.g. a duplicate declaration
read by a parser), the region is indexed again (@ref{4f3,,IndexDeclaredItems()}) after the removal.

@*Parameters: 
@code{declaredItem} (ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}) – The declared item to remove.


@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘declaredItem’ is @code{None}.

@item 
TypeError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#TypeError} – If parameter ‘declaredItem’ is not of type ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}.

@item 
@code{NotAChildError} – If parameter ‘declaredItem’ is not a declared item of this declarative region.

@item 
@code{NotInNamespaceError} – If the region is indexed, and an identifier of the declared item isn’t declared in
its namespace.

@item 
@code{NotInNamespaceError} – If the region is indexed, and an identifier of the declared item refers to another
declaration, e.g. a duplicate declaration.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
None



