@geindex ForGenerateStatement (class in pyGHDL.dom.Concurrent)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Concurrent pyGHDL dom Concurrent ForGenerateStatement}@anchor{30f}
@deffn {Class} pyGHDL.dom.Concurrent.ForGenerateStatement (generateNode, label, loopIndex, rng, declaredItems=None, statements=None, parent=None)

This class implements a @ref{3,,pyGHDL.dom} object derived from pyVHDLModel.Concurrent.ForGenerateStatement@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Concurrent.html#pyVHDLModel.Concurrent.ForGenerateStatement}.

Represents a for-generate statement.

The loop index is available as @ref{74e,,LoopIndex}, the iteration range as @ref{74f,,Range} and the
generated statements as @ref{750,,Statements}. The label is mandatory.

@cartouche
@quotation Example 
@example
  gen : for i in 0 to 3 generate
--^^^                              <- Label
--          ^                      <- LoopIndex
--               ^^^^^^            <- Range
    q(i) <= '0';
--  ^^^^^^^^^^^^                   <- Statements
  end generate;
@end example
@end quotation
@end cartouche


