@geindex ConcurrentSelectedSignalAssignment (class in pyGHDL.dom.Concurrent)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Concurrent pyGHDL dom Concurrent ConcurrentSelectedSignalAssignment}@anchor{316}
@deffn {Class} pyGHDL.dom.Concurrent.ConcurrentSelectedSignalAssignment (assignmentNode, label, target, expression, selectedWaveforms)

This class implements a @ref{3,,pyGHDL.dom} object derived from pyVHDLModel.Concurrent.ConcurrentSelectedSignalAssignment@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Concurrent.html#pyVHDLModel.Concurrent.ConcurrentSelectedSignalAssignment}.

Represents a selected concurrent signal assignment.

The selector is available as @ref{854,,Expression}, the alternatives as @ref{855,,SelectedWaveforms},
a list of SelectedWaveform@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Common.html#pyVHDLModel.Common.SelectedWaveform}. The model holds them in a list and has
no distinct field per alternative, so the markers below name list elements.

@cartouche
@quotation Example 
@example
  lbl : with sel select q <= '1' when '0', '0' when others;
--^^^                                                         <- optional Label
--           ^^^                                              <- Expression
--                      ^                                     <- Target
--                           ^^^^^^^^^^^^                     <- SelectedWaveforms[0]
--                                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^    <- SelectedWaveforms[1]
@end example
@end quotation
@end cartouche


