@geindex InsertStatement() (pyGHDL.dom.DesignUnit.Entity method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom DesignUnit pyGHDL dom DesignUnit Entity InsertStatement}@anchor{9e5}
@deffn {Method} InsertStatement (index, statement)

Insert a concurrent statement at a position of this construct.

The statement’s parent is set to this construct: a process, block or generate statement connects its namespace to
this construct’s namespace. If the statements are indexed (@ref{a0c,,IndexStatements()}), an instantiation, a block or
a generate statement is added to the lookup table matching its kind, and the statements nested in it are indexed.

A statement label is declared in the declarative region of this construct: it may neither repeat another
statement’s label, nor an identifier declared in the region, including the region an entity shares with its
architectures. An unlabeled statement declares nothing.

@*Parameters: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{index} (int@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int}) – Position, from @code{0} (first) to the number of statements (append). A negative index
counts from the end, as for list.insert()@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#list.insert}: @code{-1} inserts before the last
statement.

@item 
@code{statement} (ConcurrentStatement@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Concurrent.html#pyVHDLModel.Concurrent.ConcurrentStatement}) – The concurrent statement to insert.
@end itemize


@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘index’ is @code{None}.

@item 
TypeError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#TypeError} – If parameter ‘index’ is not of type int@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int}.

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘index’ is out of range.

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘statement’ is @code{None}.

@item 
TypeError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#TypeError} – If parameter ‘statement’ is not of type @code{ConcurrentStatement}.

@item 
@code{AlreadyInDesignError} – If parameter ‘statement’ already has a parent.

@item 
@code{DuplicateLabelError} – If the declarative region already declares the statement’s label.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
None



