@geindex IsLibraryVisible() (pyGHDL.dom.DesignUnit.Architecture method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom DesignUnit pyGHDL dom DesignUnit Architecture IsLibraryVisible}@anchor{aba}
@deffn {Method} IsLibraryVisible (libraryIdentifier)

Check if the logical name of a library is visible in this design unit.

The name @code{work} is implicitly visible, the name @code{std} too, except in a context declaration. Every other name
needs a library clause, also the real name of the working library. The library clause is searched in this design
unit’s context clause, in the context clause of its primary unit, and in the contexts these reference, also in
nested ones. The design unit must be in a library of a design.

@*Parameters: 
@code{libraryIdentifier} (str@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str}) – The normalized identifier of the library.


@*Return type: 
bool@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#bool}


@*Returns: 
@code{True}, if the library’s name is visible.

@end deffn

