@geindex RemoveContextItem() (pyGHDL.dom.DesignUnit.Architecture method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom DesignUnit pyGHDL dom DesignUnit Architecture RemoveContextItem}@anchor{a84}
@deffn {Method} RemoveContextItem (contextItem)

Remove a context item from the context clause.

The context item is detached: its parent is cleared, and it’s removed from @ref{a7f,,ContextItems} and from
@ref{a7c,,LibraryReferences}, @ref{a7d,,PackageReferences} or @ref{a7e,,ContextReferences}. The context item itself is
unchanged and can be added to another design unit, or inserted at another position.

@*Parameters: 
@code{contextItem} (@code{Union}[LibraryClause@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.LibraryClause}, UseClause@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.UseClause}, ContextReference@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.ContextReference}]) – The library clause, use clause or context reference to remove.


@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘contextItem’ is @code{None}.

@item 
TypeError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#TypeError} – If parameter ‘contextItem’ is not of type @ref{986,,LibraryClause}, @ref{987,,UseClause} or
@ref{988,,ContextReference}.

@item 
@code{NotAChildError} – If parameter ‘contextItem’ is not a context item of this design unit.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
None@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#None}


@cartouche
@quotation Attention 
The mutator doesn’t update what Analyze()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.html#pyVHDLModel.Design.Analyze} derived from the context items: the
referenced libraries, packages and contexts (@ref{a80,,ReferencedLibraries}, @ref{a81,,ReferencedPackages},
@ref{a82,,ReferencedContexts}), the namespace entries of a use clause, the edges of the dependency graph, and the
references of the symbols. A design changed after its analysis needs a new analysis.
@end quotation
@end cartouche


@subsubheading See also



@table @asis

@item @ref{a7b,,AddContextItem()}

→ Add a context item at the end of the context clause.

@item @ref{a83,,InsertContextItem()}

→ Insert a context item at a position of the context clause.
@end table

@end deffn

@geindex RemoveDeclaredItem() (pyGHDL.dom.DesignUnit.Architecture method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom DesignUnit pyGHDL dom DesignUnit Architecture RemoveDeclaredItem}@anchor{a87}
@deffn {Method} RemoveDeclaredItem (declaredItem)

Remove a declared item from the declarative region.

The declared item is detached: its parent is cleared. If the region is indexed, the declared item’s identifiers are
removed from the region’s namespace and from the lookup table matching its kind first; they are checked before
anything is changed. The declared item itself is unchanged and can be added to another declarative region, or
inserted at another position.

The namespace refers to the overload declared last: removing it, the namespace refers to the remaining overload
declared last. If another declaration shares an identifier with the declared item (e.g. a duplicate declaration
read by a parser), the region is indexed again (@ref{aa9,,IndexDeclaredItems()}) after the removal.

@*Parameters: 
@code{declaredItem} (ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}) – The declared item to remove.


@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘declaredItem’ is @code{None}.

@item 
TypeError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#TypeError} – If parameter ‘declaredItem’ is not of type ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}.

@item 
@code{NotAChildError} – If parameter ‘declaredItem’ is not a declared item of this declarative region.

@item 
@code{NotInNamespaceError} – If the region is indexed, and an identifier of the declared item isn’t declared in
its namespace.

@item 
@code{NotInNamespaceError} – If the region is indexed, and an identifier of the declared item refers to another
declaration, e.g. a duplicate declaration.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
None



@subsubheading See also



@table @asis

@item @ref{a85,,AddDeclaredItem()}

→ Add a declared item at the end of the declarative region.

@item @ref{a86,,InsertDeclaredItem()}

→ Insert a declared item at a position of the declarative region.

@item @ref{ab6,,MoveDeclaredItem()}

→ Move a declared item to a position of the declarative region.
@end table


@*Return type: 
None@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#None}


@*Parameters: 
@code{declaredItem} (ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity})

@end deffn

