@geindex Component (class in pyGHDL.dom.DesignUnit)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom DesignUnit pyGHDL dom DesignUnit Component}@anchor{989}
@deffn {Class} pyGHDL.dom.DesignUnit.Component (node, identifier, genericItems=None, portItems=None, documentation=None)

This class implements a @ref{3,,pyGHDL.dom} object derived from pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.Component@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.Component}.

Represents a component declaration.

A component declaration is a declarative region (IEEE Std 1076-2008, 12.1): its generics and ports share one
namespace, nested in the namespace of the declarative region declaring the component. A component has no declarative
part, so it has no declared items and no mutators for them.

@cartouche
@quotation Example 
@example
component ent is
  -- ...
end component;
@end example
@end quotation
@end cartouche


