→ Add a declared item at the end of the declarative region.

@item @ref{b64,,InsertDeclaredItem()}

→ Insert a declared item at a position of the declarative region.

@item @ref{b8f,,MoveDeclaredItem()}

→ Move a declared item to a position of the declarative region.
@end table


@*Return type: 
None@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#None}


@*Parameters: 
@code{declaredItem} (ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity})

@end deffn

@geindex RemoveGenericItem() (pyGHDL.dom.DesignUnit.Package method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom DesignUnit pyGHDL dom DesignUnit Package RemoveGenericItem}@anchor{b68}
@deffn {Method} RemoveGenericItem (genericItem)

Remove a generic from the generic clause.

The generic is detached: its parent and generic group are cleared and its identifiers are removed from the
language construct’s namespace, if it has one. A generic group, which becomes empty, is removed from
@ref{b82,,GenericGroups} and its parent is cleared. The generic itself is unchanged and can be added to another
language construct, or inserted at another position.

@*Parameters: 
@code{genericItem} (GenericInterfaceItemMixin@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Interface.html#pyVHDLModel.Interface.GenericInterfaceItemMixin}) – The generic to remove.


@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘genericItem’ is @code{None}.

@item 
TypeError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#TypeError} – If parameter ‘genericItem’ is not of type
GenericInterfaceItemMixin@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Interface.html#pyVHDLModel.Interface.GenericInterfaceItemMixin}.

@item 
@code{NotAChildError} – If parameter ‘genericItem’ is not a generic of this language construct.

@item 
@code{NotInNamespaceError} – If the namespace is indexed, and an identifier of the generic isn’t declared in it.

@item 
@code{NotInNamespaceError} – If the namespace is indexed, and an identifier of the generic refers to another
element, e.g. a duplicate declaration.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
None



