@geindex TypeConversion (class in pyGHDL.dom.Expression)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Expression pyGHDL dom Expression TypeConversion}@anchor{d73}
@deffn {Class} pyGHDL.dom.Expression.TypeConversion (node, targetSubtype, operand)

Represents a `type conversion', e.g. @code{integer(x)}.

@cartouche
@quotation Note 
Not reachable from this translator today. GHDL’s parser cannot tell a type conversion from an
indexed name or a function call - @code{integer(x)}, @code{arr(x)} and @code{f(x)} are all parsed as
@code{Parenthesis_Name} - and only semantic analysis rewrites one into @code{Type_Conversion}.
@ref{3,,pyGHDL.dom} parses without that pass, so a @code{Type_Conversion} node never arrives and
@code{Parenthesis_Name} is translated to
IndexedObjectOrFunctionCallSymbol@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Symbol.html#pyVHDLModel.Symbol.IndexedObjectOrFunctionCallSymbol}, which carries the ambiguity.

The constructor is kept correct so this class works if semantic analysis is ever run.
@end quotation
@end cartouche

