@geindex MoveGenericItem() (pyGHDL.dom.InterfaceItem.GenericProcedureInterfaceItem method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom InterfaceItem pyGHDL dom InterfaceItem GenericProcedureInterfaceItem MoveGenericItem}@anchor{13cd}
@deffn {Method} MoveGenericItem (genericItem, index)

Move a generic to a position of the generic clause.

The generic stays a generic of this language construct: only the order of the generic clause changes. A generic
subprogram is an overload: if the language construct’s namespace is indexed, it refers to the overload declared
last afterwards.

The generic leaves its generic group, like @ref{13aa,,RemoveGenericItem()}, and joins a generic group, like
