@geindex _FormatInterfaceItem() (pyGHDL.dom.InterfaceItem.GenericFunctionInterfaceItem method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom InterfaceItem pyGHDL dom InterfaceItem GenericFunctionInterfaceItem _FormatInterfaceItem}@anchor{1497}
@deffn {Method} _FormatInterfaceItem (mode=None, isModeView=False)

Format this interface item as a single-line declaration.

Interface items are objects, so they render like one (@code{signal p : bit}), but an object’s own
rendering cannot show the interface `mode' - a mode is not part of an object declaration. This
adds it, for the derived class’s @ref{1498,,__str__()} to return. The host class provides the object’s reserved words
@code{_OBJECT_KEYWORD}, identifiers @code{_identifiers} and subtype @code{_subtype}.

@*Parameters: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{mode} (Optional@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Optional}[Mode@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.Mode}]) – Optional, this item’s mode. Default: @code{None}, no mode declared.

@item 
@code{isModeView} (bool@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#bool}) – Optional, @code{True} if the subtype position holds a mode view (VHDL-2019), not a subtype.
Default: @code{False}.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
str@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str}


@*Returns: 
Formatted interface item.

@end deffn

