@geindex Split() (pyGHDL.dom.InterfaceItem.ParameterFileInterfaceItem method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom InterfaceItem pyGHDL dom InterfaceItem ParameterFileInterfaceItem Split}@anchor{15f9}
@deffn {Method} Split ()

Split this declaration into one declaration per identifier.

IEEE Std 1076 defines a declaration with an identifier list as equivalent to a sequence of single declarations,
one per identifier, in list order: @code{signal a, b : bit;} declares the same as @code{signal a : bit; signal b : bit;}.
This declaration keeps its first identifier. For every other identifier, a new declaration is created by
@code{Copy()}: it has its own copy of the subtype indication and of the default expression, and the same
documentation. Single declarations created before are dropped.

Without a parent, the new declarations have no parent either: the caller places them. With a parent, the parent’s
mutator splits the declaration and inserts the new declarations right after it, e.g.
WithPortsMixin.SplitPortItem@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Regions.html#pyVHDLModel.Regions.WithPortsMixin.SplitPortItem} for a port.

A declaration with one identifier is unchanged.

@*Return type: 
tuple@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#tuple}[@code{Self}, ...@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#Ellipsis}]


@*Returns: 
Tuple of declarations, one per identifier in list order, starting with this
declaration.


@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{NotAChildError} – If this declaration’s parent doesn’t list it.

@item 
@code{NotInNamespaceError} – If the parent is an indexed declarative region, and an identifier of this declaration
refers to another element, e.g. a duplicate declaration.
@end itemize

@end deffn

