@geindex CharacterEnumerationLiteral (class in pyGHDL.dom.Literal)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Literal pyGHDL dom Literal CharacterEnumerationLiteral}@anchor{1674}
@deffn {Class} pyGHDL.dom.Literal.CharacterEnumerationLiteral (node, value, documentation=None)

This class implements a @ref{3,,pyGHDL.dom} object derived from
pyVHDLModel.Expression.CharacterEnumerationLiteral@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Expression.html#pyVHDLModel.Expression.CharacterEnumerationLiteral}.

Represents an enumeration literal that is a character literal.

The literal’s character is available as @ref{16af,,Value}. It is the bare character without the enclosing apostrophes:
@code{0} for the enumeration literal @code{'0'} of @code{type bit is ('0', '1');}. This distinguishes it from an enumeration
literal named by an identifier with the same text.

@cartouche
@quotation Example 
@example
type logic is ('0', '1', 'Z');
--              ^  <- Value
@end example
@end quotation
@end cartouche

