@subsection pyGHDL.dom.Misc


@geindex module; pyGHDL.dom.Misc

This module implements derived classes for VHDL constructs not covered by another module, e.g. an alias.

`Classes'


@itemize -

@item 
@ref{17d2,,Alias}:
This class implements a @ref{3,,pyGHDL.dom} object derived from pyVHDLModel.Declaration.Alias@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Declaration.html#pyVHDLModel.Declaration.Alias}.
@end itemize


__________________________________________________________________


`Classes'

@geindex Alias (class in pyGHDL.dom.Misc)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Misc pyGHDL dom Misc Alias}@anchor{17d2}
@deffn {Class} pyGHDL.dom.Misc.Alias (node, aliasName, name, subtype=None, documentation=None)

This class implements a @ref{3,,pyGHDL.dom} object derived from pyVHDLModel.Declaration.Alias@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Declaration.html#pyVHDLModel.Declaration.Alias}.

Represents an alias declaration.

@ref{17d3,,Name} is a Symbol@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Symbol.html#pyVHDLModel.Symbol.Symbol} - like every other cross-reference in this
model - rather than a bare Name@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Name.html#pyVHDLModel.Name.Name}, so it participates in the usual
resolve-later mechanism (Reference@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Symbol.html#pyVHDLModel.Symbol.Symbol.Reference} /
IsResolved@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Symbol.html#pyVHDLModel.Symbol.Symbol.IsResolved}). Unlike @code{PackageReferenceSymbol} and similar,
there is no single fixed PossibleReference@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Symbol.html#pyVHDLModel.Symbol.PossibleReference} value that always fits: an
alias without a subtype indication can refer to almost anything nameable (an object, a type, a
subprogram, a literal, …), while an alias `with' a subtype indication can - per the LRM - only
ever refer to an object (a constant, variable, signal, or file); the @code{possibleReferences} passed
to the @code{Symbol} should reflect whichever case applies.

@cartouche
@quotation Example 
@example
alias a : bit_vector(3 downto 0) is s(3 downto 0);
--        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^     ^^^^^^^^^^^^
--        optional Subtype           Name

alias b is s;
--          ^
--          Name
@end example
@end quotation
@end cartouche

