@geindex Denote() (pyGHDL.dom.Name.AttributeName method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Name pyGHDL dom Name AttributeName Denote}@anchor{18aa}
@deffn {Method} Denote (region, place, symbol)

Determine the type or subtype this attribute name denotes as a type mark or as a part of one (IEEE Std 1076-2008,
16.2).

Depending on the predefined attribute (@ref{18ab,,PredefinedAttribute}), this name denotes:


@itemize *

@item 
@code{'subtype}: the subtype of the object its prefix denotes.

@item 
@code{'element}: the element subtype of the array type or subtype, or of the array object, its prefix denotes.

@item 
@code{'base}: the base type of the type or subtype its prefix denotes; only allowed as the prefix of another
attribute.
@end itemize

An object is an object declaration, a record element or an object alias (an alias with a subtype indication); a type
is a type or subtype declaration. The constraint of a subtype indication isn’t represented: @code{s'subtype} of
@code{signal s : bit_vector(3 downto 0)} denotes @code{bit_vector}.

@*Parameters: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{region} (DeclarativeRegionMixin@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Regions.html#pyVHDLModel.Regions.DeclarativeRegionMixin}) – The declarative region containing the type mark.

@item 
@code{place} (ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}) – The declaration containing the type mark.

@item 
@code{symbol} (Symbol@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Symbol.html#pyVHDLModel.Symbol.Symbol}) – The type mark.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
Optional@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Optional}[ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}]


@*Returns: 
The denoted type or subtype, or @code{None} if it can’t be resolved (reported as
a warning).


@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{UnhandledCriticalWarningError} – If the prefix of @code{'subtype} isn’t an object, or the object’s subtype isn’t
resolved, and no @code{WarningCollector} collects the
UnresolvedTypeMarkWarning@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Exception.html#pyVHDLModel.Exception.UnresolvedTypeMarkWarning}.

@item 
@code{UnhandledCriticalWarningError} – If the prefix of @code{'element} isn’t an array, or the array’s element type
isn’t resolved, and no @code{WarningCollector}
collects the UnresolvedTypeMarkWarning@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Exception.html#pyVHDLModel.Exception.UnresolvedTypeMarkWarning}.

@item 
@code{UnhandledCriticalWarningError} – If @code{'base} is the type mark itself, or its prefix isn’t a type, or its
base type isn’t resolved, and no
@code{WarningCollector} collects the
UnresolvedTypeMarkWarning@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Exception.html#pyVHDLModel.Exception.UnresolvedTypeMarkWarning}.

@item 
@code{UnhandledCriticalWarningError} – If the attribute denotes no type, and no
@code{WarningCollector} collects the
UnresolvedTypeMarkWarning@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Exception.html#pyVHDLModel.Exception.UnresolvedTypeMarkWarning}.
@end itemize

@end deffn

