@geindex Denote() (pyGHDL.dom.Name.OpenName method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Name pyGHDL dom Name OpenName Denote}@anchor{18ee}
@deffn {Method} Denote (region, place, symbol)

Determine the model entity this name denotes as a part of a type mark, which is an attribute name.

The type mark is an attribute name like @code{rec.f'subtype}. A name resolves its prefix first and applies itself to
the entity the prefix denotes, which must be of a kind the name can be applied to. A kind of name, which denotes no
declaration (e.g. an indexed name @code{m(0)} or @code{ptr.all}), isn’t supported and is reported.

@*Parameters: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{region} (DeclarativeRegionMixin@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Regions.html#pyVHDLModel.Regions.DeclarativeRegionMixin}) – The declarative region containing the type mark.

@item 
@code{place} (ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}) – The declaration containing the type mark.

@item 
@code{symbol} (Symbol@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Symbol.html#pyVHDLModel.Symbol.Symbol}) – The type mark.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
Optional@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Optional}[ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}]


@*Returns: 
The denoted model entity, or @code{None} if it can’t be resolved (reported as a
warning).


@*Raises: 
@code{UnhandledCriticalWarningError} – If this kind of name isn’t supported as a part of a type mark, and no
@code{WarningCollector} collects the
UnresolvedTypeMarkWarning@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Exception.html#pyVHDLModel.Exception.UnresolvedTypeMarkWarning}.

@end deffn

