`Classes'

@geindex Design (class in pyGHDL.dom.NonStandard)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom NonStandard pyGHDL dom NonStandard Design}@anchor{1d9}
@deffn {Class} pyGHDL.dom.NonStandard.Design (name=None, vhdlVersion=2008, tabSize=8)

This class implements a @ref{3,,pyGHDL.dom} object derived from pyVHDLModel.Design@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.html#pyVHDLModel.Design}.

A @code{Design} represents set of VHDL libraries as well as all loaded and analysed source files (see Document@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.html#pyVHDLModel.Document}).

It’s the root of this code document-object-model (CodeDOM). It contains at least one VHDL library (see Library@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.html#pyVHDLModel.Library}). When the design is
analysed (see @ref{190d,,Analyze()}), multiple graph data structures will be created and populated with vertices and edges. As a first result, the design’s compile
order and hierarchy can be iterated. As a second result, the design’s `top-level' is identified and referenced from the design (see @ref{190e,,TopLevel}).

The `design' contains references to the following graphs:


@itemize *

@item 
@ref{190f,,DependencyGraph}

@item 
@ref{1910,,CompileOrderGraph}

@item 
@ref{1911,,HierarchyGraph}

@item 
@ref{1912,,ObjectGraph}
@end itemize

