@geindex LinkContextReferences() (pyGHDL.dom.NonStandard.Design method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom NonStandard pyGHDL dom NonStandard Design LinkContextReferences}@anchor{1933}
@deffn {Method} LinkContextReferences ()

Link all context references (context clause) to the matching context.

@*Return type: 
None@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#None}


@subsubheading Algorithm



@enumerate 

@item 
Iterate all design units:


@itemize *

@item 
Iterate all context references in the design unit:


@itemize *

@item 
Iterate each context symbol within the context reference.


@enumerate 

@item 
Get the library identifier from the symbol.

@item 
Get the context identifier from the symbol.

@item 
Resolve library:


@itemize *

@item 
If library name is @code{work}, get library from design unit.

@item 
If library name isn’t visible (IsLibraryVisible()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.DesignUnit.IsLibraryVisible}), raise an
exception.

@item 
Otherwise, lookup library by name in design.
@end itemize

@item 
Resolve context:


@itemize *

@item 
Lookup context by name in library.
@end itemize

@item 
Update design unit:


@itemize *

@item 
Update the context symbol’s target with the referenced context.

@item 
Add an entry in the design unit’s @code{_referencedContexts} dictionary referencing the referenced context.

@item 
Add an edge in the dependency graph from design unit to the referenced context.
@end itemize
@end enumerate
@end itemize
@end itemize

@item 
Iterate all context vertices in the dependency graph (@code{_dependencyGraph}) in topological order:


@itemize *

@item 
Get the context from the context vertex.

@item 
Iterate all predecessor vertices (design unit vertices) of the context vertex:


@enumerate 

@item 
Get the design unit from design unit vertex.

@item 
Iterate referenced libraries of the context:


@itemize *

@item 
Add an entry in the design unit’s @code{_referencedLibraries} dictionary referencing the referenced library.

@item 
Add an empty dictionary in the design unit’s @code{_referencedPackages} dictionary.
@end itemize

@item 
Iterate referenced packages of the context:


@itemize *

@item 
Add an entry in the design unit’s @code{_referencedPackages} dictionary referencing the referenced package.
@end itemize
@end enumerate
@end itemize

@item 
Iterate all design units with a namespace, the contexts they reference and, transitively, the contexts these
reference: import the declarations, which @ref{1930,,LinkContexts()} imported into the namespace of a context, into the
design unit’s namespace.
@end enumerate


@subsubheading See also



@table @asis

@item @ref{1931,,LinkLibraryReferences()}

Link `library clause'.

@item @ref{1932,,LinkPackageReferences()}

Link `use clause'.

@item @ref{1926,,AnalyzeDependencies()}

Analyze dependencies and link relations.
@end table


@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{ContextReferenceLibraryNotVisibleError} – If a context reference references a library, whose name isn’t
visible
(IsLibraryVisible()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.DesignUnit.IsLibraryVisible}).

@item 
@code{ContextNotFoundError} – If a context reference references a context, which doesn’t exist in
its library.

@item 
@code{UseClauseNotLinkedError} – If a use clause of a referenced context isn’t linked. 
Call @ref{1930,,LinkContexts()} before.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
None

@end deffn

@geindex LinkContexts() (pyGHDL.dom.NonStandard.Design method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom NonStandard pyGHDL dom NonStandard Design LinkContexts}@anchor{1930}
@deffn {Method} LinkContexts ()

Resolves and links all items (library clauses, use clauses and nested context references) in contexts.

It iterates all contexts in the design. Therefore, the library of the context is used as the working library. By
default, the working library is implicitly referenced in
@code{_referencedLibraries}. In addition, a new empty dictionary is created in
@code{_referencedPackages} and
@code{_referencedContexts} for that working library.

At first, all library clauses are resolved (a library clause my have multiple library reference symbols). For each
referenced library an entry in @code{_referencedLibraries} is generated and new
empty dictionaries in @code{_referencedPackages} and
@code{_referencedContexts} for that working library. In addition, a vertex in
the dependency graph is added for that relationship.

The library clauses of all contexts are resolved before the use clauses of any context.

At second, all use clauses are linked as the use clauses of a design unit’s context clause (a use clause may have
multiple package member reference symbols). 
→ @ref{194c,,_LinkUseClause()}

The declarations they make potentially visible are imported into the context’s namespace. The design units
referencing the context import them from there (@ref{1933,,LinkContextReferences()}).

@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{ReferencedLibraryNotExistingError} – If a library clause references a library, which doesn’t exist in the
design.

@item 
@code{UseClauseLibraryNotVisibleError} – If a use clause references a library, whose name isn’t visible
(IsLibraryVisible()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.DesignUnit.IsLibraryVisible}).

@item 
@code{PackageNotFoundError} – If a use clause references a package, which doesn’t exist in its
library.

@item 
@code{UnknownSymbolKindError} – If the type of a symbol in a use clause is unknown.

@item 
@code{PackageInstantiationNotLinkedError} – If a use clause names a package instantiation, which isn’t linked to its
generic package. 
Call @ref{192f,,LinkPackageInstances()} before.

@item 
@code{UnhandledCriticalWarningError} – If a use clause names a package member, which the package doesn’t
declare, a primary unit, which the library doesn’t contain, a prefix,
which isn’t a visible package, or an uninstantiated generic package, and
no @code{WarningCollector} collects the
UnresolvedNameWarning@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Exception.html#pyVHDLModel.Exception.UnresolvedNameWarning}.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
None@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#None}

@end deffn

@geindex LinkLibraryReferences() (pyGHDL.dom.NonStandard.Design method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom NonStandard pyGHDL dom NonStandard Design LinkLibraryReferences}@anchor{1931}
@deffn {Method} LinkLibraryReferences ()

Link all library references (library clause) to the matching VHDL library.

@*Return type: 
None@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#None}


@subsubheading Algorithm



@enumerate 

@item 
Iterate all design units with contexts:


@itemize *

@item 
If the design unit is a primary unit:


@enumerate 

@item 
Iterate all library identifiers in @code{DEFAULT_LIBRARIES} (@code{std}):


@itemize *

@item 
Get the referenced library by name from the design.

@item 
Add an entry in the design unit’s @code{_referencedLibraries} dictionary referencing the referenced library.

@item 
Add an empty dictionary in the design unit’s @code{_referencedPackages} dictionary.

@item 
Add an empty dictionary in the design unit’s @code{_referencedContexts} dictionary.

@item 
Add an edge in the dependency graph from design unit to the referenced library.
@end itemize

@item 
Get the design unit’s library, unless it’s a library in @code{DEFAULT_LIBRARIES}:


@itemize *

@item 
Add an entry in the design unit’s @code{_referencedLibraries} dictionary referencing the referenced library.

@item 
Add an empty dictionary in the design unit’s @code{_referencedPackages} dictionary.

@item 
Add an empty dictionary in the design unit’s @code{_referencedContexts} dictionary.

@item 
Add an edge in the dependency graph from design unit to the referenced library.
@end itemize
@end enumerate

@item 
If the design unit is a secondary unit:


@itemize *

@item 
If design unit is an architecture, get the corresponding entity’s referenced libraries.

@item 
If design unit is a package body, get the corresponding package’s referenced libraries.

@item 
Otherwise, raise an exception
@end itemize

For every referenced library create new dictionary entries in the design unit’s @code{_referencedLibraries}.
@end itemize

@item 
Iterate every library reference (library clause) in the design unit:


@itemize *

@item 
Iterate every library symbol within the library reference:


@itemize *

@item 
Get the library identifier from the symbol.

@item 
Continue the inner loop, if identifier is @code{work}.

@item 
Get the referenced library from the design or raise an exception.

@item 
Update the library symbol’s target with the referenced library.

@item 
Add an entry in the design unit’s @code{_referencedLibraries} dictionary referencing the referenced library.

@item 
Add an empty dictionary in the design unit’s @code{_referencedPackages} dictionary.

@item 
Add an empty dictionary in the design unit’s @code{_referencedContexts} dictionary.

@item 
Add an edge in the dependency graph from design unit to the referenced library.
@end itemize
@end itemize
@end enumerate


@subsubheading See also



@table @asis

@item @ref{1932,,LinkPackageReferences()}

Link `use clause'.

@item @ref{1933,,LinkContextReferences()}

Link `context clause'.

@item @ref{1926,,AnalyzeDependencies()}

Analyze dependencies and link relations.
@end table


@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{LibraryNotFoundError} – If library @code{std} isn’t loaded. 
Call @ref{194d,,LoadStdLibrary()} before.

@item 
@code{UnknownSecondaryUnitKindError} – If a secondary unit is neither an architecture nor a package body.

@item 
@code{LibraryClauseLibraryNotFoundError} – If a library clause references a library, which doesn’t exist in the
design.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
None

@end deffn

