@deffn {Method} ResetAnalysis ()

Reset everything an analysis (@ref{190d,,Analyze()}) derived, so the design can be analyzed again.

Everything built by the user is kept: libraries, documents, design units, declarations and the declarations in
namespaces. Lookup tables built by indexing (e.g. @ref{1929,,IndexPackages()}) are kept too, as indexing again yields
the same lookup tables. Resetting a design, which wasn’t analyzed, changes nothing.

@*Return type: 
None@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#None}


@subsubheading Algorithm



@enumerate 

@item 
Delete the dependency, compile-order, hierarchy and object graph (@code{Delete()}), so
their vertices and edges are freed at once, replace them by empty graphs, and forget the top-level.

@item 
Clear the references to vertices of all libraries, documents and design units.

@item 
Clear the references of all design units: referenced libraries, packages and contexts, the symbols of library
clauses, use clauses and context references, and the items imported into namespaces. Use clauses in declarative
regions nested in a design unit are cleared too, as are the references of type marks and alias names
(@ref{1937,,ResolveTypeMarks()}) and the base types of subtypes; a subtype of a predefined library
(@ref{1956,,Library.IsPredefined}) keeps its base type.

@item 
Unlink architectures from entities and package bodies from packages: an entity’s architectures, a package’s
body, the symbols referencing the entity or package, and the link to the parent namespace.

@item 
Unlink package instantiations from their generic package: the symbol and the components copied from it.

@item 
Unbind all components: their entity and blackbox state.

@item 
Clear the symbols of entity and component instantiations.
@end enumerate
@end deffn

