@geindex ResolveTypeMarks() (pyGHDL.dom.NonStandard.Design method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom NonStandard pyGHDL dom NonStandard Design ResolveTypeMarks}@anchor{1937}
@deffn {Method} ResolveTypeMarks ()

Resolve the type marks of all declarations in the design.

It’s the first step of @ref{1936,,AnalyzeObjects()}, after the use clauses are linked. Each type mark is looked up at its
place (LookupName()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Regions.html#pyVHDLModel.Regions.DeclarativeRegionMixin.LookupName}), so the visibility rules apply: e.g. a type
declared after the place isn’t visible, and conflicting use clauses make a type mark ambiguous. A resolved type mark
references the type, the subtype or the generic type (Reference@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Symbol.html#pyVHDLModel.Symbol.Symbol.Reference}); a type mark
denoting an alias of a type references the type. Resolving again yields the same references, as long as the design
isn’t changed; after a change, @ref{190d,,Analyze()} links the use clauses again.

@*Return type: 
None@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#None}


@subsubheading Algorithm



@enumerate 

@item 
Iterate the design units of the predefined libraries (@ref{1956,,Library.IsPredefined}), then the design units of all
documents in compile order (the compile-order graph, @code{ComputeCompileOrder()}), so a package is resolved
before its users.

@item 
Iterate the declarative regions of each design unit, the outermost first
(IterateDeclarationRegions()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Regions.html#pyVHDLModel.Regions.DeclarativeRegionMixin.IterateDeclarationRegions}):


@enumerate 

@item 
Index the declared items of a region not indexed yet, e.g. a process or a subprogram.

@item 
Iterate the region’s declarations in declaration order; each resolves its references
(ResolveReferences()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity.ResolveReferences}):


@itemize *

@item 
Every declaration resolves its type marks (IterateTypeMarks()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity.IterateTypeMarks}) by the
region looking them up (ResolveTypeMark()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Regions.html#pyVHDLModel.Regions.DeclarativeRegionMixin.ResolveTypeMark}).

@item 
An incomplete type reports, if no full type declaration follows in its region
(ResolveReferences()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Type.html#pyVHDLModel.Type.AnonymousType.ResolveReferences}).

@item 
An alias without a subtype indication resolves its name
(ResolveReferences()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Declaration.html#pyVHDLModel.Declaration.Alias.ResolveReferences}).

@item 
A subtype sets its base type (BaseType@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Type.html#pyVHDLModel.Type.Subtype.BaseType}): the resolved type, or the base
type of the resolved subtype.
@end itemize
@end enumerate
@end enumerate


@subsubheading See also



@table @asis

@item @ref{1955,,ResetAnalysis()}

Reset everything an analysis derived, including the references of type marks.
@end table


@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{UnhandledCriticalWarningError} – If a type mark can’t be resolved, and no
@code{WarningCollector} collects the
UnresolvedTypeMarkWarning@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Exception.html#pyVHDLModel.Exception.UnresolvedTypeMarkWarning}.

@item 
@code{UnhandledCriticalWarningError} – If the name of an alias can’t be resolved, and no
@code{WarningCollector} collects the
UnresolvedNameWarning@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Exception.html#pyVHDLModel.Exception.UnresolvedNameWarning}.

@item 
@code{UnhandledCriticalWarningError} – If an incomplete type has no full type declaration, and no
@code{WarningCollector} collects the
IncompleteTypeWarning@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Exception.html#pyVHDLModel.Exception.IncompleteTypeWarning}.

@item 
@code{UnhandledCriticalWarningError} – If an identifier is declared twice in a declarative region and no
@code{WarningCollector} collects the
DuplicateDeclarationWarning@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Exception.html#pyVHDLModel.Exception.DuplicateDeclarationWarning}.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
None

@end deffn

