@geindex _LinkUseClause() (pyGHDL.dom.NonStandard.Design method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom NonStandard pyGHDL dom NonStandard Design _LinkUseClause}@anchor{194c}
@deffn {Method} _LinkUseClause (designUnit, namespace, useClause, isContextItem)

Link the symbols of a use clause and import the declarations they make potentially visible into a namespace.

@subsubheading Algorithm


Iterate every package symbol within the use clause (a use clause can have multiple comma-separated symbols):


@enumerate 

@item 
Get the package name from the symbol: the symbol’s name for a @code{PackageReferenceSymbol} (@code{use lib.pkg;}), else
its prefix (@code{use lib.pkg.all;}, @code{use lib.pkg.item;}). Get the library name, the prefix of the package name.
If the symbol is neither of the three package symbol types, raise an exception.

@item 
If the use clause names a library (@code{use work.all;}, @code{use lib.unit;}, the prefix is @code{work} or the visible
name of a library (IsLibraryVisible()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.DesignUnit.IsLibraryVisible}), and @code{unit} isn’t a package
of it):


@itemize *

@item 
@code{.all}: import all primary units of the library (entities, packages, configurations, contexts).

@item 
@code{.unit}: import the primary unit of that name; if there is none, raise an
UnresolvedNameWarning@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Exception.html#pyVHDLModel.Exception.UnresolvedNameWarning}.
@end itemize

Continue with the next symbol.

@item 
Resolve the package:


@itemize *

@item 
Without a library name (@code{use pkg.all;}): lookup the directly visible package at the use clause
(Lookup()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Namespace.html#pyVHDLModel.Namespace.Namespace.Lookup}), e.g. made visible by @code{use lib.pkg;} or declared in an
enclosing region. If there is none, raise an UnresolvedNameWarning@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Exception.html#pyVHDLModel.Exception.UnresolvedNameWarning} and continue
with the next symbol.

@item 
With a library name: if library name is @code{work}, get the library of the design unit; if library name isn’t
visible (IsLibraryVisible()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.DesignUnit.IsLibraryVisible}), raise an exception; otherwise lookup
the library by name in the design.
Lookup the package by name in the library; if it doesn’t exist, raise an exception.
@end itemize

@item 
Update the design unit:


@itemize *

@item 
Update the package symbol’s reference with the package.

@item 
If the package was named with its library and the use clause is an item of the design unit’s context clause,
add an entry in the design unit’s @code{_referencedPackages} dictionary.

@item 
If the package was named with its library, add an edge in the dependency graph from design unit to the package.
@end itemize

@item 
If the package is an uninstantiated generic package, raise an
UnresolvedNameWarning@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Exception.html#pyVHDLModel.Exception.UnresolvedNameWarning} and continue with the next symbol.

@item 
Import the public package members into the namespace (AddImport()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Namespace.html#pyVHDLModel.Namespace.Namespace.AddImport}), each
with the use clause as origin:


@itemize *

@item 
@code{AllPackageMembersReferenceSymbol} (@code{use lib.pkg.all;}): every declaration of the package, incl. the
enumeration literals and physical units of its types
(IterateDeclarations()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.Package.IterateDeclarations}).

@item 
@code{PackageMemberReferenceSymbol} (@code{use lib.pkg.item;}): every declaration of the package with the identifier
@code{item}, e.g. all overloads of a subprogram, and the enumeration literals and physical units of a type or of a
subtype’s base type (IterateMemberDeclarations()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.Package.IterateMemberDeclarations}). If there is none,
raise an UnresolvedNameWarning@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Exception.html#pyVHDLModel.Exception.UnresolvedNameWarning}.

@item 
@code{PackageReferenceSymbol} (@code{use lib.pkg;}): the package itself.
@end itemize
@end enumerate

@*Parameters: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{designUnit} (DesignUnit@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.DesignUnit}) – The design unit containing the use clause.

@item 
@code{namespace} (Namespace@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Namespace.html#pyVHDLModel.Namespace.Namespace}) – The namespace of the declarative region or of the context declaration
containing the use clause.

@item 
@code{useClause} (UseClause@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.UseClause}) – The use clause.

@item 
@code{isContextItem} (bool@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#bool}) – @code{True}, if the use clause is an item of the design unit’s context
clause.
@end itemize


@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{UseClauseLibraryNotVisibleError} – If a use clause references a library, whose name isn’t visible
(IsLibraryVisible()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.DesignUnit.IsLibraryVisible}).

@item 
@code{PackageNotFoundError} – If a use clause references a package, which doesn’t exist in its
library.

@item 
@code{UnknownSymbolKindError} – If the type of a symbol in the use clause is unknown.

@item 
@code{PackageInstantiationNotLinkedError} – If a package instantiation isn’t linked to its generic package.

@item 
@code{UnhandledCriticalWarningError} – If a use clause names a package member, which the package doesn’t
declare, a primary unit, which the library doesn’t contain, a prefix,
which isn’t a visible package, or an uninstantiated generic package, and
no @code{WarningCollector} collects the
UnresolvedNameWarning@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Exception.html#pyVHDLModel.Exception.UnresolvedNameWarning}.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
None@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#None}

@end deffn

