@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom NonStandard pyGHDL dom NonStandard Library DenoteBy}@anchor{196e}
@deffn {Method} DenoteBy (name, region, place, symbol)

Determine the model entity a name denoting this declaration denotes, as a part of a type mark (Name.Denote@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Name.html#pyVHDLModel.Name.Name.Denote}).

A declaration, which a name in a type mark can denote, overrides this method and returns itself: an object, an
alias, a type or subtype, a record element, a package. Any other declaration (e.g. a subprogram) is reported.

@*Parameters: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{name} (Name@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Name.html#pyVHDLModel.Name.Name}) – The name denoting this declaration, a part of the type mark.

@item 
@code{region} (DeclarativeRegionMixin@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Regions.html#pyVHDLModel.Regions.DeclarativeRegionMixin}) – The declarative region containing the type mark.

@item 
@code{place} (ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}) – The declaration containing the type mark.

@item 
@code{symbol} (Symbol@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Symbol.html#pyVHDLModel.Symbol.Symbol}) – The type mark.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
Optional@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Optional}[ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}]


@*Returns: 
@code{None}, as a name in a type mark can’t denote this declaration (reported
as a warning).


@*Raises: 
