@geindex LinkArchitectures() (pyGHDL.dom.NonStandard.Library method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom NonStandard pyGHDL dom NonStandard Library LinkArchitectures}@anchor{1982}
@deffn {Method} LinkArchitectures ()

Link all architectures to corresponding entities.

@*Return type: 
None@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#None}


@subsubheading Algorithm



@enumerate 

@item 
Iterate all architecture groups (grouped per entity symbol’s name).


@itemize *

@item 
Check if entity symbol’s name exists as an entity in this library.
@end itemize


@enumerate 

@item 
For each architecture in the same architecture group:


@itemize *

@item 
Add architecture to entities architecture dictionary pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.Entity._architectures@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.Entity._architectures}.

@item 
Assign found entity to architecture’s entity symbol pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.Architecture._entity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.Architecture._entity}

@item 
Set parent namespace of architecture’s namespace to the entitie’s namespace.

@item 
Add an edge in the dependency graph from the architecture’s corresponding dependency vertex to the entity’s corresponding dependency vertex.
@end itemize
@end enumerate
@end enumerate

@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{ArchitectureEntityNotFoundError} – If entity name doesn’t exist.

@item 
@code{ArchitectureExistsInLibraryError} – If architecture name already exists for entity.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
None



@subsubheading See also



@table @asis

@item @ref{1983,,LinkPackageBodies()}

Link all package bodies to corresponding packages.

@item @ref{1984,,LinkPackageInstances()}

Link all package instances to corresponding generic packages.
@end table

@end deffn

@geindex LinkPackageBodies() (pyGHDL.dom.NonStandard.Library method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom NonStandard pyGHDL dom NonStandard Library LinkPackageBodies}@anchor{1983}
@deffn {Method} LinkPackageBodies ()

Link all package bodies to corresponding packages.

@*Return type: 
None@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#None}


@subsubheading Algorithm



@enumerate 

@item 
Iterate all package bodies.


@itemize *

@item 
Check if package body symbol’s name exists as a package in this library.

@item 
Report a DuplicateDeclarationWarning@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Exception.html#pyVHDLModel.Exception.DuplicateDeclarationWarning}, if the package has another package body.

@item 
Add package body to package pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.Package._packageBody@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.Package._packageBody}.

@item 
Assign found package to package body’s package symbol pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.PackageBody._package@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.PackageBody._package}

@item 
Set parent namespace of package body’s namespace to the package’s namespace.

@item 
Add an edge in the dependency graph from the package body’s corresponding dependency vertex to the package’s corresponding dependency vertex.
@end itemize
@end enumerate

@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{PackageBodyPackageNotFoundError} – If package name doesn’t exist.

@item 
@code{UnhandledCriticalWarningError} – If a package has another package body, which is replaced, and no
@code{WarningCollector} collects the
DuplicateDeclarationWarning@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Exception.html#pyVHDLModel.Exception.DuplicateDeclarationWarning}.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
None



