@geindex RemoveContextItem() (pyGHDL.dom.PSL.VerificationMode method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom PSL pyGHDL dom PSL VerificationMode RemoveContextItem}@anchor{1b5c}
@deffn {Method} RemoveContextItem (contextItem)

Remove a context item from the context clause.

The context item is detached: its parent is cleared, and it’s removed from @ref{1b57,,ContextItems} and from
@ref{1b54,,LibraryReferences}, @ref{1b55,,PackageReferences} or @ref{1b56,,ContextReferences}. The context item itself is
unchanged and can be added to another design unit, or inserted at another position.

@*Parameters: 
@code{contextItem} (@code{Union}[LibraryClause@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.LibraryClause}, UseClause@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.UseClause}, ContextReference@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.ContextReference}]) – The library clause, use clause or context reference to remove.


@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘contextItem’ is @code{None}.

@item 
TypeError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#TypeError} – If parameter ‘contextItem’ is not of type @code{LibraryClause}, @code{UseClause} or
@code{ContextReference}.

@item 
@code{NotAChildError} – If parameter ‘contextItem’ is not a context item of this design unit.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
None@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#None}


@cartouche
@quotation Attention 
The mutator doesn’t update what Analyze()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.html#pyVHDLModel.Design.Analyze} derived from the context items: the
referenced libraries, packages and contexts (@ref{1b58,,ReferencedLibraries}, @ref{1b59,,ReferencedPackages},
@ref{1b5a,,ReferencedContexts}), the namespace entries of a use clause, the edges of the dependency graph, and the
references of the symbols. A design changed after its analysis needs a new analysis.
@end quotation
@end cartouche


