@geindex ElsifBranch (class in pyGHDL.dom.Sequential)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Sequential pyGHDL dom Sequential ElsifBranch}@anchor{1bd9}
@deffn {Class} pyGHDL.dom.Sequential.ElsifBranch (branchNode, condition, statements=None)

This class implements a @ref{3,,pyGHDL.dom} object derived from pyVHDLModel.Sequential.ElsifBranch@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Sequential.html#pyVHDLModel.Sequential.ElsifBranch}.

Represents an @code{elsif} branch of an if statement.

The branch’s condition is available as @ref{1c1d,,Condition}, its body as @ref{1c1e,,Statements}.
An if statement may have any number of them.

@cartouche
@quotation Example 
The whole if statement is shown; the bracket marks the part this class represents.

@example
if sel = '0' then
  s <= '0';
elsif sel = '1' then  -- ┐ ElsifBranch
--    ^^^^^^^^^       -- │   <- Condition
  s <= '1';           -- │
--^^^^^^^^^           -- ┘   <- Statements
else
  s <= '0';
end if;
@end example
@end quotation
@end cartouche

