@geindex IfStatement (class in pyGHDL.dom.Sequential)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Sequential pyGHDL dom Sequential IfStatement}@anchor{1bdb}
@deffn {Class} pyGHDL.dom.Sequential.IfStatement (ifNode, ifBranch, elsifBranches=None, elseBranch=None, label=None)

This class implements a @ref{3,,pyGHDL.dom} object derived from pyVHDLModel.Sequential.IfStatement@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Sequential.html#pyVHDLModel.Sequential.IfStatement}.

Represents an if statement.

An if statement has one @code{if} branch (@ref{1bd8,,IfBranch}), any number of @code{elsif} branches
(@ref{1c67,,ElsIfBranches}) and an optional @code{else} branch (@ref{1bda,,ElseBranch}).

@cartouche
@quotation Example 
Only an @code{if} branch:

@example
  lbl : if sel = '0' then
--^^^                       <- optional Label
    s <= '0';
  end if;
@end example

With @code{elsif} and @code{else} branches:

@example
  lbl : if sel = '0' then
--^^^                       <- optional Label
--      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^   <- IfBranch
    s <= '0';
  elsif sel = '1' then
--^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^      <- ElsIfBranches[0]
    s <= '1';
  else
--^^^^                      <- ElseBranch
    s <= '0';
  end if;
@end example
@end quotation
@end cartouche


