@geindex InsertStatement() (pyGHDL.dom.Sequential.WhileLoopStatement method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Sequential pyGHDL dom Sequential WhileLoopStatement InsertStatement}@anchor{1d7e}
@deffn {Method} InsertStatement (index, statement)

Insert a sequential statement at a position of this construct.

The statement’s parent is set to this construct.

Every label of a process or subprogram body is declared in the process’ or subprogram’s declarative region: the
statement’s label and the labels of statements nested in it (in branches, case alternatives and loops) may neither
repeat another label of the body, nor an identifier declared in the region. A construct not in a process or
subprogram (yet) checks the labels of its own statements. An unlabeled statement declares nothing.

@*Parameters: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{index} (int@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int}) – Position, from @code{0} (first) to the number of statements (append). A negative index
counts from the end, as for list.insert()@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#list.insert}: @code{-1} inserts before the last
statement.

@item 
@code{statement} (SequentialStatement@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Sequential.html#pyVHDLModel.Sequential.SequentialStatement}) – The sequential statement to insert.
@end itemize


@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘index’ is @code{None}.

@item 
TypeError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#TypeError} – If parameter ‘index’ is not of type int@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int}.

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘index’ is out of range.

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘statement’ is @code{None}.

@item 
TypeError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#TypeError} – If parameter ‘statement’ is not of type @code{SequentialStatement}.

@item 
@code{AlreadyInDesignError} – If parameter ‘statement’ already has a parent.

@item 
@code{DuplicateLabelError} – If the declarative region already declares a label of the statement.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
None



