@geindex Function (class in pyGHDL.dom.Subprogram)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Subprogram pyGHDL dom Subprogram Function}@anchor{408}
@deffn {Class} pyGHDL.dom.Subprogram.Function (node, functionName, returnType, isPure=True, genericItems=None, parameterItems=None, declaredItems=None, statements=None, documentation=None)

This class implements a @ref{3,,pyGHDL.dom} object derived from pyVHDLModel.Subprogram.Function@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Subprogram.html#pyVHDLModel.Subprogram.Function}.

Represents a function.

A function returns a value of its return type (@ref{1fca,,ReturnType}) and is either pure or impure
(@ref{1fcb,,IsPure}). Besides its parameters, it has its own declarative part (@ref{1fcc,,DeclaredItems})
and statements (@ref{1fcd,,Statements}).

@cartouche
@quotation Example 
@example
function fun(constant c : in positive) return integer is
--       ^^^                                               <- Identifier
--           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^                      <- ParameterItems
--                                            ^^^^^^^      <- ReturnType
  variable tmp : integer;
--^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^                                  <- DeclaredItems
begin
  tmp := c;
--^^^^^^^^^                                                <- Statements
  return tmp;
end function;
@end example
@end quotation
@end cartouche


