Insert a parameter at a position of the parameter list.

The parameter’s parent is set to this language construct, and its identifiers are added to the language construct’s
namespace, if it has one.

Without a parameter group, the parameter joins the parameter group of the parameter before @code{index}; at index
@code{0}, the parameter group of the first parameter. If there are no parameters, the parameter forms a new unnamed
parameter group. A parameter group given must contain @code{index} or end at it, so the parameter groups stay
contiguous.

