@geindex LookupName() (pyGHDL.dom.Subprogram.ProcedureMethod method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Subprogram pyGHDL dom Subprogram ProcedureMethod LookupName}@anchor{219b}
@deffn {Method} LookupName (place, symbol, name, warningType)

Look up the declarations a simple name or an expanded name denotes at a place in this region.

A simple name is looked up at the place (Lookup()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Namespace.html#pyVHDLModel.Namespace.Namespace.Lookup}). An expanded name
@code{pkg.T} or @code{lib.pkg.T} resolves its prefix: @code{pkg} to a package visible at the place, else to an enclosing
declarative region of that name (e.g. the package or entity containing the place); @code{lib.pkg} by the library
(@code{work} or a library whose name is visible in the design unit containing the place,
IsLibraryVisible()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.html#pyVHDLModel.DesignUnit.DesignUnit.IsLibraryVisible}) and the package’s name. Then the suffix is searched
among the declarations of the package or region (FindDeclarations()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Namespace.html#pyVHDLModel.Namespace.Namespace.FindDeclarations}).

A failure is reported as a warning of the given type, whose label names the kind of name in the message
(e.g. @code{Type mark}); then no declaration is returned. A name, which is a part of the symbol’s name (e.g. the prefix
@code{s} of the type mark @code{s'subtype}), is reported as a prefix of the symbol’s name.

@*Parameters: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{place} (ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}) – The declaration containing the name.

@item 
@code{symbol} (Symbol@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Symbol.html#pyVHDLModel.Symbol.Symbol}) – The symbol containing the name.

@item 
@code{name} (Name@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Name.html#pyVHDLModel.Name.Name}) – The simple name or expanded name: the symbol’s name or a part of it.

@item 
@code{warningType} (type@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#type}[UnresolvedNameWarning@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Exception.html#pyVHDLModel.Exception.UnresolvedNameWarning}]) – The warning class reporting a failure.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
tuple@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#tuple}[ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}, ...@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#Ellipsis}]


@*Returns: 
Tuple of the directly visible declarations, empty if none is.


@*Raises: 
@code{UnhandledCriticalWarningError} – If the name isn’t visible, is ambiguous, or has a prefix, which isn’t a
visible package or an enclosing region, and no
@code{WarningCollector} collects the warning.

@end deffn

@geindex MoveDeclaredItem() (pyGHDL.dom.Subprogram.ProcedureMethod method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Subprogram pyGHDL dom Subprogram ProcedureMethod MoveDeclaredItem}@anchor{218c}
@deffn {Method} MoveDeclaredItem (declaredItem, index)

Move a declared item to a position of the declarative region.

The declared item stays a declared item of this declarative region: only the order of the declared items changes.

If the region is indexed, the lookup tables and the namespace follow the new order: a list of overloads (e.g. in
@code{Functions}) follows the declaration order, and the namespace refers to the overload declared last. If
another declaration shares an identifier with the declared item (e.g. a duplicate declaration read by a parser),
the region is indexed again (@ref{2189,,IndexDeclaredItems()}) after the move.

@*Parameters: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{declaredItem} (ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}) – The declared item to move.

@item 
@code{index} (int@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int}) – Position of the declared item after the move, from @code{0} (first) to the number of
declared items minus one (last). A negative index counts from the end, as for a
list@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#list} index: @code{-1} moves the declared item to the end.
@end itemize


@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘declaredItem’ is @code{None}.

@item 
TypeError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#TypeError} – If parameter ‘declaredItem’ is not of type ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}.

@item 
@code{NotAChildError} – If parameter ‘declaredItem’ is not a declared item of this declarative region.

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘index’ is @code{None}.

@item 
TypeError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#TypeError} – If parameter ‘index’ is not of type int@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int}.

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘index’ is out of range.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
None



