@geindex SplitDeclaredItem() (pyGHDL.dom.Subprogram.FunctionInstantiation method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Subprogram pyGHDL dom Subprogram FunctionInstantiation SplitDeclaredItem}@anchor{2242}
@deffn {Method} SplitDeclaredItem (declaredItem)

Split a declared item with an identifier list into one declaration per identifier.

The declared item keeps its first identifier. For every other identifier, a new declaration is created by its
@code{Copy()} and inserted right after it, in list order; its parent is set to this declarative region. If the region
is indexed, the namespace and lookup table entries of the other identifiers refer to the new declarations; they
are checked before anything is changed. A declared item declaring one identifier is unchanged.

@*Parameters: 
@code{declaredItem} (ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}) – The declared item to split.


@*Return type: 
tuple@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#tuple}[ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}, ...@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#Ellipsis}]


@*Returns: 
Tuple of declarations, one per identifier in list order, starting with the split
declared item.


@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘declaredItem’ is @code{None}.

@item 
TypeError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#TypeError} – If parameter ‘declaredItem’ is not of type ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}.

@item 
@code{NotAChildError} – If parameter ‘declaredItem’ is not a declared item of this declarative region.

@item 
@code{NotInNamespaceError} – If the region is indexed, and an identifier of the declared item refers to another
declaration, e.g. a duplicate declaration.
@end itemize



@subsubheading See also



@table @asis

@item Split()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.MultipleNamedEntityMixin.Split}

