@geindex InsertDeclaredItem() (pyGHDL.dom.Subprogram.ProcedureInstantiation method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Subprogram pyGHDL dom Subprogram ProcedureInstantiation InsertDeclaredItem}@anchor{2281}
@deffn {Method} InsertDeclaredItem (index, declaredItem)

Insert a declared item at a position of the declarative region.

The declared item’s parent is set to this declarative region. If the region is indexed, its identifiers are added
to the region’s namespace and to the lookup table matching its kind.

An identifier is declared once per declarative region: interface items and declared items count, including those of
the language construct sharing the declarative region (an entity and its architecture, a package and its body).
Subprograms are overloadable: a subprogram may share its identifier with other subprograms. A protected type body
may share its identifier with its protected type, a full type with its incomplete type declaration, and a constant
with its deferred constant. Items imported into the namespace (e.g. by a use clause) are hidden.

@*Parameters: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{index} (int@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int}) – Position, from @code{0} (first) to the number of declared items (append).
A negative index counts from the end, as for list.insert()@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#list.insert}: @code{-1}
inserts before the last declared item.

@item 
@code{declaredItem} (ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}) – The declared item to insert.
@end itemize


@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘index’ is @code{None}.

@item 
TypeError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#TypeError} – If parameter ‘index’ is not of type int@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int}.

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘index’ is out of range.

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘declaredItem’ is @code{None}.

@item 
TypeError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#TypeError} – If parameter ‘declaredItem’ is not a declaration allowed in this declarative
region.

@item 
@code{AlreadyInDesignError} – If parameter ‘declaredItem’ already has a parent.

@item 
@code{DuplicateDeclarationError} – If an existing declaration of the declarative region shares an
identifier with the declared item.
@end itemize


@*Return type: 
None



