@geindex MoveGenericItem() (pyGHDL.dom.Subprogram.ProcedureInstantiation method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Subprogram pyGHDL dom Subprogram ProcedureInstantiation MoveGenericItem}@anchor{22aa}
@deffn {Method} MoveGenericItem (genericItem, index)

Move a generic to a position of the generic clause.

The generic stays a generic of this language construct: only the order of the generic clause changes. A generic
subprogram is an overload: if the language construct’s namespace is indexed, it refers to the overload declared
last afterwards.

The generic leaves its generic group, like @ref{2288,,RemoveGenericItem()}, and joins a generic group, like
@ref{2287,,InsertGenericItem()} without a generic group: the generic group of the generic before its new position; at
index @code{0}, the generic group of the first generic. A move to the generic’s current position changes nothing.

@*Parameters: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{genericItem} (GenericInterfaceItemMixin@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Interface.html#pyVHDLModel.Interface.GenericInterfaceItemMixin}) – The generic to move.

@item 
@code{index} (int@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int}) – Position of the generic after the move, from @code{0} (first) to the length of
@ref{22a0,,GenericItems} minus one (last). A negative index counts from the end, as for a
list@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#list} index: @code{-1} moves the generic to the end.
@end itemize


@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘genericItem’ is @code{None}.

@item 
TypeError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#TypeError} – If parameter ‘genericItem’ is not of type
GenericInterfaceItemMixin@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Interface.html#pyVHDLModel.Interface.GenericInterfaceItemMixin}.

@item 
@code{NotAChildError} – If parameter ‘genericItem’ is not a generic of this language construct.

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘index’ is @code{None}.

@item 
TypeError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#TypeError} – If parameter ‘index’ is not of type int@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int}.

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘index’ is out of range.

@item 
@code{NotInNamespaceError} – If the namespace is indexed, and the identifier of a generic subprogram refers to an
element, which is no overload, e.g. a duplicate declaration.
