@geindex AggregateSymbol (class in pyGHDL.dom.Symbol)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Symbol pyGHDL dom Symbol AggregateSymbol}@anchor{230e}
@deffn {Class} pyGHDL.dom.Symbol.AggregateSymbol (aggregateNode, targets)

This class implements a @ref{3,,pyGHDL.dom} object derived from pyVHDLModel.Symbol.AggregateSymbol@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Symbol.html#pyVHDLModel.Symbol.AggregateSymbol}.

Represents a group of targets written as an aggregate on the left-hand side of an assignment.

VHDL’s grammar calls it an aggregate (@code{target ::= name | aggregate}), but it decomposes the assigned value into its
targets: each element is a target itself, e.g. a variable or a signal, never a constant. The group has no name of its
own (Name@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Symbol.html#pyVHDLModel.Symbol.Symbol.Name} is @code{None}); its targets are available as @ref{2403,,Targets}, the group
is their parent.

@cartouche
@quotation Example 
@example
(carry, sum) := add(a, b);
-- ^^^^^^^^^^^^    <- the aggregate symbol
--  ^^^^^  ^^^    <- Targets
@end example
@end quotation
@end cartouche

