@geindex ConstrainedScalarSubtypeSymbol (class in pyGHDL.dom.Symbol)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Symbol pyGHDL dom Symbol ConstrainedScalarSubtypeSymbol}@anchor{2313}
@deffn {Class} pyGHDL.dom.Symbol.ConstrainedScalarSubtypeSymbol (node, subtypeName, rng)

This class implements a @ref{3,,pyGHDL.dom} object derived from pyVHDLModel.Symbol.ConstrainedScalarSubtypeSymbol@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Symbol.html#pyVHDLModel.Symbol.ConstrainedScalarSubtypeSymbol}.

Represents a reference to a scalar subtype narrowed by a range.

The referenced language entity is available as @ref{2562,,Reference} once resolved. The range is
mandatory: a type mark without a range constraint is a SimpleSubtypeSymbol@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Symbol.html#pyVHDLModel.Symbol.SimpleSubtypeSymbol}.

@cartouche
@quotation Example 
@example
for i in integer range 0 to 3 loop
--       ^^^^^^^                     <- Name
--                     ^^^^^^        <- Constraint
@end example

A range constraint written as a range attribute is a RangeFromName@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.RangeFromName}
referring to a RangeAttributeSymbol@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Symbol.html#pyVHDLModel.Symbol.RangeAttributeSymbol}:

@example
subtype index is natural range vector'range;
--               ^^^^^^^                      <- Name
--                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^   <- Constraint
@end example
@end quotation
@end cartouche

