@geindex ArrayElementConstraint (class in pyGHDL.dom.Symbol)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Symbol pyGHDL dom Symbol ArrayElementConstraint}@anchor{2316}
@deffn {Class} pyGHDL.dom.Symbol.ArrayElementConstraint (node, constraints)

This class implements a @ref{3,,pyGHDL.dom} object derived from pyVHDLModel.Symbol.ArrayElementConstraint@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Symbol.html#pyVHDLModel.Symbol.ArrayElementConstraint}.

Represents the constraint of an array element in a record constraint: one range per dimension.

The ranges are available as @ref{25c5,,Constraints}. The constraint has no type mark of its own: the element’s type is
the subtype of the record element (IEEE Std 1076-2008, 6.3: @code{element_constraint ::= array_constraint |
record_constraint}).

@cartouche
@quotation Example 
@example
signal s : rec_t(data(7 downto 0), m(0 to 1, 0 to 7));
--                    ^^^^^^^^^^                         <- Constraints
--                                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^      <- Constraints
@end example
@end quotation
@end cartouche


