@geindex RecordElementConstraint (class in pyGHDL.dom.Symbol)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Symbol pyGHDL dom Symbol RecordElementConstraint}@anchor{2317}
@deffn {Class} pyGHDL.dom.Symbol.RecordElementConstraint (node, constraints)

This class implements a @ref{3,,pyGHDL.dom} object derived from pyVHDLModel.Symbol.RecordElementConstraint@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Symbol.html#pyVHDLModel.Symbol.RecordElementConstraint}.

Represents the constraint of a record element in a record constraint: a nested record constraint.

The element constraints are available as @ref{25dc,,Constraints}. The constraint has no type mark of its own: the
element’s type is the subtype of the record element (IEEE Std 1076-2008, 6.3: @code{element_constraint ::=
array_constraint | record_constraint}).

@cartouche
@quotation Example 
@example
signal s : rec_t(inner(field(3 downto 0)));
--                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^      <- Constraints
@end example
@end quotation
@end cartouche


