@geindex IndexedObjectOrFunctionCallSymbol (class in pyGHDL.dom.Symbol)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Symbol pyGHDL dom Symbol IndexedObjectOrFunctionCallSymbol}@anchor{231b}
@deffn {Class} pyGHDL.dom.Symbol.IndexedObjectOrFunctionCallSymbol (node, name)

This class implements a @ref{3,,pyGHDL.dom} object derived from pyVHDLModel.Symbol.IndexedObjectOrFunctionCallSymbol@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Symbol.html#pyVHDLModel.Symbol.IndexedObjectOrFunctionCallSymbol}.

Represents a reference that is either an indexed object, a function call or a type conversion.

The referenced language entity is available as @ref{2648,,Reference} once resolved.

@cartouche
@quotation Attention 
All three are written the same way - @code{arr(0)}, @code{f(0)} and @code{integer(0)} are indistinguishable
as syntax, so a parser produces one shape for them and only name resolution tells them apart.
@end quotation
