@geindex PhysicalUnit (class in pyGHDL.dom.Type)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Type pyGHDL dom Type PhysicalUnit}@anchor{266b}
@deffn {Class} pyGHDL.dom.Type.PhysicalUnit (node, identifier, value=None, documentation=None)

This class implements a @ref{3,,pyGHDL.dom} object derived from pyVHDLModel.Type.PhysicalUnit@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Type.html#pyVHDLModel.Type.PhysicalUnit}.

Represents a unit declaration of a physical type: its primary unit or one of its secondary units.

A unit name is declared by the physical type’s declaration in the declarative region enclosing the type, so it’s
visible like the type itself, e.g. imported by a use clause. The unit’s parent is its physical type; the unit is the
parent of its value.

@cartouche
@quotation Example 
@example
type distance is range 0 to 1000000 units
  um;
--^^                                        <- Identifier (primary unit)
  mm = 1000 um;
--^^                                        <- Identifier (secondary unit)
--   ^^^^^^^                                <- Value
end units;
@end example
@end quotation
@end cartouche

