@geindex ResolveTypeMark() (pyGHDL.dom.Type.ProtectedTypeBody method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Type pyGHDL dom Type ProtectedTypeBody ResolveTypeMark}@anchor{2813}
@deffn {Method} ResolveTypeMark (place, symbol)

Resolve a type mark at its place in this region and set the symbol’s reference.

@subsubheading Algorithm



@enumerate 

@item 
Clear the symbol’s reference.

@item 
Look up the type mark’s name (@ref{2804,,LookupName()}).

@item 
An alias of a type is replaced by the type its name references.

@item 
If the declaration is a type, a subtype or a generic type, it becomes the symbol’s reference. A full type, which
follows the place in the same region, is visible by its incomplete type declaration only to an access type.
@end enumerate

An attribute name denoting a type (e.g. @code{s'subtype}, @code{A'element}) is resolved part by part
(Denote()@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Name.html#pyVHDLModel.Name.Name.Denote}); the type it denotes becomes the symbol’s reference.

@*Parameters: 

@itemize *

@item 
@code{place} (ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}) – The declaration containing the type mark.

@item 
@code{symbol} (SubtypeSymbol@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Symbol.html#pyVHDLModel.Symbol.SubtypeSymbol}) – The type mark.
@end itemize


@*Raises: 
@code{UnhandledCriticalWarningError} – If the type mark isn’t visible, is ambiguous, has a prefix, which isn’t a
visible package, denotes no type, or denotes an incomplete type outside of an
access type, and no @code{WarningCollector} collects
the UnresolvedTypeMarkWarning@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Exception.html#pyVHDLModel.Exception.UnresolvedTypeMarkWarning}.


@*Return type: 
None@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#None}

@end deffn

@geindex SplitDeclaredItem() (pyGHDL.dom.Type.ProtectedTypeBody method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom Type pyGHDL dom Type ProtectedTypeBody SplitDeclaredItem}@anchor{2814}
@deffn {Method} SplitDeclaredItem (declaredItem)

Split a declared item with an identifier list into one declaration per identifier.

The declared item keeps its first identifier. For every other identifier, a new declaration is created by its
@code{Copy()} and inserted right after it, in list order; its parent is set to this declarative region. If the region
is indexed, the namespace and lookup table entries of the other identifiers refer to the new declarations; they
are checked before anything is changed. A declared item declaring one identifier is unchanged.

@*Parameters: 
@code{declaredItem} (ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}) – The declared item to split.


@*Return type: 
tuple@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#tuple}[ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}, ...@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#Ellipsis}]


@*Returns: 
Tuple of declarations, one per identifier in list order, starting with the split
declared item.


@*Raises: 

@itemize *

@item 
ValueError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError} – If parameter ‘declaredItem’ is @code{None}.

@item 
TypeError@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#TypeError} – If parameter ‘declaredItem’ is not of type ModelEntity@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Base.html#pyVHDLModel.Base.ModelEntity}.

@item 
@code{NotAChildError} – If parameter ‘declaredItem’ is not a declared item of this declarative region.

@item 
@code{NotInNamespaceError} – If the region is indexed, and an identifier of the declared item refers to another
declaration, e.g. a duplicate declaration.
@end itemize



