@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom _Translate pyGHDL dom _Translate GetModeViewElementsFromChainedNodes}@anchor{28ac}
@deffn {Function} pyGHDL.dom._Translate.GetModeViewElementsFromChainedNodes (nodeChain)

Translates a chain of mode view elements (IIR nodes) to a sequence of
pyVHDLModel.Interface.ModeViewElement@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.Interface.html#pyVHDLModel.Interface.ModeViewElement}.

@*Parameters: 
@code{nodeChain} (Iir) – The IIR node representing the first mode view element in the chain.


@*Return type: 
Generator[ModeViewElement, None, None]


@*Returns: 
A generator returning mode view elements.


@cartouche
@quotation Note 
Unlike declarations/interface items (where the `last' node in a @code{Has_Identifier_List} group owns
the shared subtype/value and earlier ones are Null), mode view elements are the other way around:
the `first' node in the group (@code{Has_Identifier_List == True}) owns the real @code{Mode}/
@code{Mode_View_Name} - subsequent nodes only contribute their identifier, ending with the node where
@code{Has_Identifier_List} becomes @code{False}. Verified against real GHDL analysis for
@code{x, y : out;}: @code{x} has @code{Has_Identifier_List=True}, @code{Mode=out}; @code{y} has
@code{Has_Identifier_List=False}, @code{Mode=<unset>}.
@end quotation
@end cartouche
@end deffn

