@geindex GetDocumentationOfDesignUnit() (in module pyGHDL.dom._Utils)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom _Utils pyGHDL dom _Utils GetDocumentationOfDesignUnit}@anchor{28b8}
@deffn {Function} pyGHDL.dom._Utils.GetDocumentationOfDesignUnit (unitNode)

Collects the doc-comment lines of a design unit (entity, architecture, package, …).

In IIR, a design unit is a @code{Design_Unit} node holding the context clause and the unit’s declaration (the
@code{Library_Unit}), as in IEEE Std 1076, 13.1. A design unit’s documentation consists of the comments `libghdl'
attached to the @code{Design_Unit} node (the comments before the unit, except the file header), followed by the
comments attached to the declaration node itself. A nested package has no @code{Design_Unit} node, so only its own
comments are read.

@*Parameters: 
@code{unitNode} (TypeVar@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.TypeVar}(@code{Iir}, bound= c_int@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/library/ctypes.html#ctypes.c_int})) – The IIR node of the unit’s declaration (entity declaration, architecture body, …).


@*Return type: 
Optional@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Optional}[str@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str}]


@*Returns: 
The comment lines joined by newlines, or @code{None} if the unit has no comment.

@end deffn

