@geindex WriteGraphML() (pyGHDL.dom.formatting.GraphML.DependencyGraphFormatter method)
@anchor{pyGHDL/pyGHDL dom formatting GraphML pyGHDL dom formatting GraphML DependencyGraphFormatter WriteGraphML}@anchor{28cd}
@deffn {Method} WriteGraphML (path)

Writes the dependency graph as a GraphML file, grouping the vertices by library.

The document declares six GraphML@footnote{http://graphml.graphdrawing.org} keys, four for nodes and two for edges:


@multitable {xxxxxxxxxx} {xxxxxxxxxx} {xxxxxxxxxxxxxx} {xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx} 
@headitem

Key

@tab

Applies to

@tab

Attribute

@tab

Value

@item

@code{nd1}

@tab

node

@tab

@code{id}

@tab

The vertex’ ID, repeated as data so a reader ignoring the XML @code{id} still sees it.

@item

@code{nd2}

@tab

node

@tab

@code{value}

@tab

The label to display. An architecture is written as @code{entity(architecture)}, a document as its ID,
anything else as its identifier.

@item

@code{nd3}

@tab

node

@tab

@code{kind}

@tab

The name of the vertex’ DependencyGraphVertexKind@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.html#pyVHDLModel.DependencyGraphVertexKind}.

@item

@code{nd4}

@tab

node

@tab

@code{color}

@tab

The fill color from @ref{28cb,,NODE_COLORS}, selected by vertex kind.

@item

@code{ed3}

@tab

edge

@tab

@code{kind}

@tab

The name of the edge’s DependencyGraphEdgeKind@footnote{https://vhdl.github.io/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel/pyVHDLModel.html#pyVHDLModel.DependencyGraphEdgeKind}.

@item

@code{ed4}

@tab

edge

@tab

@code{color}

@tab

The line color from @ref{28cc,,EDGE_COLORS}, selected by edge kind.

@end multitable


A node’s XML @code{id} is the vertex’ ID from the model. An edge has none, so edges are numbered in the order they
are written and get @code{e1}, @code{e2}, …; their @code{source} and @code{target} are vertex IDs.

The graph is `grouped into one subgraph per library': an enclosing node @code{grp_<library>} holds a nested
@code{<graph id="<library>">} with that library’s vertices. A vertex is assigned to a library by asking the model -
a library vertex for itself, a document vertex through its first design unit, anything else through its own
@code{Library}. Edges are written afterwards at the top level, so an edge may cross from one subgraph into another.

@*Parameters: 
@code{path} (Path@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/library/pathlib.html#pathlib.Path}) – The path of the file to write.

@end deffn

