@section pyGHDL.lib


@geindex module; pyGHDL.lib

Resource package containing GHDL’s binary artifacts.

This package holds no Python code. It is the install location of the files produced when GHDL is
built, so that a pyGHDL wheel is self-contained and @ref{1b,,pyGHDL.libghdl} finds the shared library
next to itself instead of somewhere on the system.

`Contents of an installed package:'


@multitable {xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx} {xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx} 
@headitem

File or directory

@tab

Purpose

@item

@code{libghdl-*.so}, @code{libghdl-*.dll}, @code{libghdl-*.dylib}

@tab

GHDL’s analyzer and simulator as a shared library, loaded by @ref{1b,,pyGHDL.libghdl} through
ctypes@footnote{https://docs.python.org/3/library/ctypes.html#module-ctypes}. The filename carries GHDL’s version, e.g. @code{libghdl-7_0_0_dev.so}.

@item

@code{libgnat-*.so}

@tab

The GNAT runtime @code{libghdl} was linked against, shipped when it is not expected to be present on the
target system.

@item

@code{libghdlvpi.*}

@tab

The VPI support library, used by simulations loading VPI modules.

@item

@code{ghdl/}

@tab

The pre-analyzed VHDL libraries - @code{std} and @code{ieee} for each supported language revision
(@code{v87}, @code{v93}, @code{v08}, @code{v19}) - plus their sources in @code{ghdl/src}.

@end multitable


@cartouche
@quotation Note 
The files are build output: none of them is in version control, and the directory contains only
this module in a source checkout. They appear when GHDL is installed or a wheel is unpacked.
@end quotation
@end cartouche

