@subsection Fields


Every field of every node is read and written by a @code{Get_}/@code{Set_} pair. A field means the same thing on every kind
that has it, so it is described here once and the node pages link back to this page.

The access column says how the link is held:


@itemize *

@item 
`owned' - The node owns the referenced node.

@item 
`ref' - A reference to a node owned elsewhere.

@item 
`maybe ref' - A reference if @code{Is_Ref} is set, otherwise owned.

@item 
`of ref' - The elements of the list are references.

@item 
`of maybe ref' - The elements are references if @code{Is_Ref} is set.

@item 
`forward ref' - A reference resolved only by semantic analysis.

@item 
`maybe forward ref' - A forward reference if @code{Is_Forward_Ref}.

@item 
`chain' - The head of a chain of nodes linked by @code{Get_Chain}.

@item 
`chain next' - The next element of the chain this node belongs to.
@end itemize

The node diagrams use the same names, drawn as edge colours:

@menu
