@subsubsection Iir_Kind_Library_Clause


LRM08 13.2 Design libraries

@example
library_clause ::= LIBRARY logical_name_list ;
@end example

@example
logical_name_list ::= logical_name @{ , logical_name @}
@end example

@example
logical_name ::= identifier
@end example

Note: a library_clause node is created for every logical_name. As a consequence, the scope of the library starts after
the logical_name and not after the library_clause.  However, since an identifier can only be used as a logical_name, and
since the second occurrence has no effect, this is correct.

