@node Iir_Kind_Procedure_Declaration,,,Subprogram Declaration
@anchor{internals/ast/23-subprogram-declaration iir-kind-procedure-declaration}@anchor{37d0}@anchor{internals/ast/23-subprogram-declaration int-ast-procedure-declaration}@anchor{37d1}
@subsubsection Iir_Kind_Procedure_Declaration


LRM08 4.2 Subprogram declarations

@example
subprogram_declaration ::= subprogram_specification ;
@end example

@example
subprogram_specification ::=
   procedure_specification | function_specification
@end example

@example
procedure_specification ::=
   PROCEDURE designator
      subprogram_header
      [ [ PARAMETER ] ( formal_parameter_list ) ]
@end example

@example
function_specification ::=
   [ PURE | IMPURE ] FUNCTION designator
      subprogram_header
      [ [ PARAMETER ] ( formal_parameter_list ) ] RETURN type_mark
@end example

@example
designator ::= identifier | operator_symbol
@end example

@example
operator_symbol ::= string_literal
@end example

Note: the subprogram specification of a body is kept, but should be ignored if there is a subprogram declaration.  The
function Is_Second_Subprogram_Specification returns True on such specification.

